/**
 * English search index for the settings directory.
 *
 * The directory's titles, breadcrumbs, aliases, and keywords stay Chinese: they are search
 * identities rather than rendered copy, and a Chinese query must keep matching them. That
 * leaves an English device unable to find a setting by its English name, because the catalog
 * has no English text to match against.
 *
 * This table is that missing text. It maps each Chinese identity to the English value of the
 * resource the render sinks already use, so `SettingsDestinationCatalog` can index both
 * languages and an English query still lands on the right row. It is a plain string map on
 * purpose: the catalog compiles its index without a `resourceManager`, so it cannot read
 * `app.string` itself.
 *
 * The localization guard checks every entry against `base` and `en_US`, so a regenerated
 * table cannot drift from the catalogs.
 */
